<p align="center"><img border="0" src="http://www.breneware.com/paseq/BWbanner2a.gif" width="350" height="55"></p>
<p align="center">&nbsp;&nbsp; <u> <font size="7">ShowEQ</font></u></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p align="left"><b><font size="5">1. <font color="#FF0000">What is ShowEQ?</font></font><font face="Cooper Black" size="5"><font color="#FF0000">&nbsp;</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;
</font></b></p>
<p align="left"><font color="#FF0000"><b><font face="Cooper Black" size="5">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</font><font face="Times New Roman" size="4">&nbsp;</font></b></font><font face="Times New Roman" size="4">ShowEQ 
is a 2D electronic map in realtime that is displayed on a second computer. It 
lists everything in the zone you are currently in. MoB's, Players, Merchants. Everything you 
need to navigate the zone.</font></p>
<p align="left"><b><font face="Times New Roman" size="5">2. 
<font color="#FF0000">How does it work?</font></font></b></p>
<p align="left"><b><font face="Times New Roman" size="5">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</font></b><font size="4" face="Times New Roman">ShowEQ 
is a packet sniffer that monitors the Everquest client traffic. It is completely 
passive and undetectable.</font></p>
<p align="left"><b><font face="Times New Roman" size="5">3. 
<font color="#FF0000">What do I need to 
run it?</font></font></b></p>
<p align="left">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
<font size="4">Winning this auction 
gets you the computer running RedHat 9.0 Linux with ShowEQ installed. The computer will 
normally be a Pentium 200 PC or better. You have to supply your own monitor, 
keyboard and mouse. You also have to have the proper network to support ShowEQ. 
</font></p>
<p align="left"><font size="4">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; This means your network needs to look like this:</font></p>
<p align="left"><font size="4" color="#FF0000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Cable/DSL 
Modem ---- Hub ---- ShowEQ box</font></p>
<p align="left"><font size="4" color="#FF0000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 
|</font></p>
<p align="left"><font size="4" color="#FF0000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 
EQ Box&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </font></p>
<p align="left"><font size="4">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Please 
remember, there is a difference between a &quot;hub&quot; and a &quot;switch&quot;. It must be a 
hub. I can also supply one if needed, see the bottom of the auction for other 
services.</font></p>
<p align="left"><b><font face="Times New Roman" size="5">4. 
<font color="#FF0000">What do I see when 
using ShowEQ?</font></font></b></p>
<p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="5"><b>&nbsp;&nbsp; </b>&nbsp;&nbsp;
</font><font face="Times New Roman" size="4">&nbsp; Here is a picture of 
Greater Fay using ShowEQ.</font></p>
<p align="left"><img border="0" src="http://www.breneware.com/paseq/showeq.jpg" width="1000" height="800"></p>
<p align="left"><b><font face="Times New Roman" size="5">5. 
<font color="#FF0000">How do I update 
ShowEQ if it breaks?</font></font></b></p>
<p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><b>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</b>I will also include a script to update ShowEQ in the 
event that it is broken via patch. It will be as simple as double clicking an 
icon. </font></p>
<p align="left"><b><font face="Times New Roman" size="5">6. 
<font color="#FF0000">How fast can I get one?</font></font></b></p>
<p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 
No need to wait for the auction to end. Email me if you want one, and I will 
start another auction for you with a buy it now option. Once payment is made, I 
can ship UPS ground or faster depending on what you want. It usually takes me 2 
working days to build and box it up for shipment. I usually have at least 1 on 
hand, ready to ship.</font></p>
<p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="5">Other services offered:</font></p>
<p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4" color="#FF0000">Keyboard, 
mouse and monitor: +$100.00 and shipping</font></p>
<p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4" color="#FF0000">Hub: +$45 
and shipping</font></p>
<p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4" color="#FF0000">Dialup ShowEQ boxes: 
+$75.00 (for those of you who do not have DSL or Cable)</font></p>
<p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4" color="#FF0000">Spawn Alerts: +$75.00 
(This includes a sound card and a config file that alerts you when a rare has 
spawned)</font></p>
<p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="5">Tech Support: </font>
<font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><b>Free Email 
tech support is always available.</b></font></p>
<p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="5"><font color="#FF0000">Custom Computers: 
</font>Want to 
do more then just run ShowEQ or browse the web? I can also add a WebServer, 
Email Server, FTP server, you name it. On a &quot;as-requested&quot; basis for pricing.</font></p>
<p align="left"><u><b><font face="Times New Roman" size="4">Buyer pays all 
shipping costs. We accept personal checks, Money orders, Western Union and 
Paypal (for verified Paypal accounts only).</font></b></u></p>
<p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="5">If you have any questions, 
please do not hesitate to ask!</font></p>

